source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:627ead0d267d6685e54243e2271a73568df3cfa78414486be6772455a8fa9499","file":"preprints/The-equivariant-cohomological-Hikita-conjecture-for-arbitrary-quivers-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":78,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"e1f4d9e9d82752a59499a2cf302b15571b316a43483094360f6ca7f8be1e6a6d","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-equivariant-cohomological-Hikita-conjecture-for-arbitrary-quivers-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:627ead0d267d6685e54243e2271a73568df3cfa78414486be6772455a8fa9499","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-equivariant-cohomological-Hikita-conjecture-for-arbitrary-quivers-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L78"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every datum \\eqref{eq:gauge-data}, every commuting flavor torus $F$, and\nevery regular stability character $\\nu$, both coefficient maps are\nsurjective and have the same kernel.  They therefore induce a canonical\nisomorphism of graded\n$R$-algebras\n\\[\n H_F^*(X;\\C)\\ \\cong\\ \\C[Y_{\\mathfrak f}^{\\nu}].\n\\]\nThe gradings are ordinary cohomological degree and BFN homological degree,\nrespectively.  The assertion includes the empty case, whose ring is zero."}
